# Titan Orbit — Windows late-join crash invariants

Relay late-join with hundreds of map ghosts hard-crashes the **Windows client**. Fixes keep getting undone by unrelated agents. **Do not regress these invariants.**

Paired: `titan-orbit-ship-simulation.mdc`, embedded NetCode (`Packages/com.unity.netcode`), `tools/netcode-patches/`.

---

## Root cause (proven in Player.log)

| Symptom | Cause |
|---------|--------|
| `Crash!!!` right after `[JoinSettle] TransformSystemGroup RE-ENABLED` | Disabling LTW during Instantiates of ~700 asteroids, then flipping the group back on → Burst LocalToWorld flood (2026-07-18 12:17) |
| `Crash!!!` in `DrawAsteroids` / `MarkFromQuery` / `MinimapEcsEntitySync` → `ToEntityArray` | Gathering all asteroids during Instantiates / settle |
| `baseline for a ghost we do not have` | Deferring placeholders without `SpawnedGhostEntityMap` registration |

**Patterns that must never return:**
1. Disable → re-enable `TransformSystemGroup` / `LocalToWorldSystem` around join Instantiates.
2. Any `ToEntityArray` / `WithEntityAccess` over asteroids/planets/gems while `ClientJoinSettleCache.Settling`.

---

## Non-negotiable rules

### 1. Embedded GhostSpawn patch (git)

- NetCode is **`file:com.unity.netcode`** under `Titan Orbit/Packages/com.unity.netcode`.
- Patch id: `TO_GhostSpawn_v9_transformsAlwaysOn` (or newer).
- Canonical: `tools/netcode-patches/GhostSpawnSystem.cs` + pre-build guard.
- **Required:** safe snapshot copy, no Burst on `OnUpdate`, **1 Instantiates/frame**, stock placeholder CreateEntity (ghost-map safe).
- **Forbidden:** placeholder defer+requeue without map registration; PackageCache-only edits; Instantiates cap removed; Instantiates flood.

### 2. Join settle — hybrid/UI gate ONLY

- `TitanOrbitClientJoinTransformGateSystem` sets `ClientJoinSettleCache.Settling` from GhostSpawn backlog.
- **`TransformSystemGroup` / `LocalToWorldSystem` must stay ENABLED always.** The settle system must force them on if a bad build left them off.
- **Forbidden:** disable TransformSystemGroup during settle (causes re-enable Crash!!!).
- Instantiates safety = Instantiates 1/frame with LTW warm, not “freeze transforms then thaw.”
- **While `Settling == true`, ALL of these must no-op or use Pending-only small queues:**
  - `EcsWorldVisualizer` full asteroid/planet `ToEntityArray` creates
  - `MapBodyHybridVisualRequestSystem` (also no-op if placeholders / spawn buffer non-empty)
  - **`MinimapEcsEntitySync`** (and any new minimap/radar/UI ECS sync)
  - Moon collider mass CreateEntity
  - Any new MonoBehaviour that queries all map ghosts

### 3. Hybrid map visuals + loading bar

- Bake `MapBodyHybridVisualPending` on client planet/asteroid/gem ghosts (`GhostPrefabType.Client`).
- `MapBodyHybridVisualRequestSystem` = post-settle orphan catcher only.
- Visualizer drains Pending during settle (budget-capped); full scans only after settle.
- **Loading:** `MapSessionMetaRpc` = `N`; bar = `MapLoadingProxyCount` (GO Instantiates only).
- **Forbidden:** Instantiates-only progress; `MarkFromQuery` / map-body `ToEntityArray` during settle.

### 4. UI / other agents — common regression

```csharp
if (ClientJoinSettleCache.Settling)
    return;
```

Never `ToEntityArray` all asteroids during settle.

### 5. Do not “simplify” these away

Verify Windows Relay late-join with 400+ asteroids after every client rebuild.

